// Constructing a record literal that supplies a value for an ARRAY-typed field
// has no route. Reduced from `samples/cli/systems/wire_protocol`.
//
//   R { samples: [0, 0, 0, 0] }   (field `[i32; 4]`)   OMITTED (this fixture)
//   R { inner: Inner { v: 1 } }   (nested-record field) checks
//   R { v: 1 }                    (scalar field)        checks
//   let a: [i32; 4] = [1, 2, 3, 4];                     checks
//
// The array value does not have to be written inline: filling the field from a
// VARIABLE omits identically, so it is the record literal having to supply an
// array-typed field, not the array literal expression. A bare array literal
// bound to an array local checks, which is the control that separates the two.
//
// Ruled out, each against its own control: `FixedVec`, generics and const
// generics (the reduction has none); NESTING, which the sample's shape invites
// -- a flat record omits and a nested-RECORD field is the clean checking
// control; the negative values the sample spells `0 - 2`; array length and
// element type (`[i32; 4]`, `[i32; 1]`, `[u8; 4]` all omit); passing the local
// by `&`/`&mut` and using it after the call; and having an array-typed field at
// all -- a record whose array field is never literal-constructed checks, as
// does one written by element assignment.
//
// The label depends on where the literal is constructed, not on what declined:
// a `let` local reports `statement sequence: local data: structural call
// binding` and a self-field store of the same literal reports `structural field
// store: record literal source`. Neither string names an array or a record
// literal field. Do not pin a repair on either.
//
// ADJACENT but distinct, and the controls say so: in
// `tests/omega/pending/collections/element_policy_array_literal_store` a whole
// array literal stored into an array FIELD checks when the element is plain and
// omits only under an element arithmetic policy. Here the element is plain
// `i32` and it omits anyway, because the array is being supplied through a
// record literal. Three composite gaps now sit beside each other -- that one, 
// this one, and `tests/omega/pending/structs/policy_field_record_local_read`.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Packet {
    samples: [i32; 4];
}

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    let packet: Packet = Packet { samples: [0, 0, 0, 0] };
    self.console.exit_process(0);
}
